- `app/auth.py:6-11` — `require_api_key` now returns `HTTPException(401)` for missing or unknown `X-API-Key`, otherwise returns the username from `VALID_API_KEYS`.
- `app/main.py:17-31` — `GET /tasks` filters by `status` (enum), `priority` (exact match), `assigned_to` (all optional, combinable), then paginates with `page`/`page_size` (defaults 1/20, `Query(ge=1)` guards negative slices).
- `app/main.py:42-50` — `POST /tasks` (201): requires auth, 404s on unknown `project_id`, generates ID via `max(task.id)+1`.
- `app/main.py:53-64` — `PUT /tasks/{task_id}`: requires auth, partial updates via `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so unspecified fields are preserved, 404 when not found.
- `app/main.py:67-75` — `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` (204): requires auth, 404 when not found.

**Verification:** the challenge's own check script passes 9/9 (`EXCELLENT` rubric), and extra edge cases pass: priority filter, combined filters, page 2, PUT/DELETE 404s, partial-PUT field preservation, explicit `assigned_to: null`, 422 on invalid enum / `page=0`, 401 on unauthenticated PUT/DELETE, default `page_size`.
